\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday through Thursday evening\nproducing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 22 at 9:44AM MDT until September 25 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, San Juan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon through late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The ground remains saturated from recent heavy rainfall over the\npast week. After a brief break, deep moisture is expected to\nreturn to southwest Colorado Tuesday with a few inches of\nrainfall possible during the Wednesday through Thursday\ntimeframe. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday through Thursday evening\nproducing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Animas River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-22T11:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 221122 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 522 AM MDT Tue Sep 22 